('BANKED_CLOZE',
 '<p>The pervasive influence of social media on modern society cannot be <b>1._____</b>. Platforms such as Facebook, Instagram, and TikTok have fundamentally altered how people communicate, consume information, and form opinions. While these platforms offer unprecedented opportunities for <b>2._____</b> and self-expression, they also present significant challenges.</p><p>Research has shown that excessive social media use can <b>3._____</b> to feelings of anxiety, depression, and social isolation, particularly among young people. The constant exposure to carefully curated <b>4._____</b> of others lives can lead to unhealthy comparisons and diminished self-esteem. Moreover, the spread of <b>5._____</b> on these platforms has become a major concern, with false narratives often spreading faster than factual information. To address these issues, experts recommend establishing healthy digital <b>6._____</b>, such as limiting screen time and engaging in more face-to-face interactions. Educational institutions are increasingly <b>7._____</b> digital literacy programs into their curricula to help students navigate the online world more effectively. The goal is not to <b>8._____</b> technology but to develop a more mindful and <b>9._____</b> approach to its use. Ultimately, the responsibility lies with both platforms and users to create a more <b>10._____</b> digital environment.</p>',
 '[{"label":"A","text":"denied"},{"label":"B","text":"connection"},{"label":"C","text":"contribute"},{"label":"D","text":"portrayals"},{"label":"E","text":"misinformation"},{"label":"F","text":"boundaries"},{"label":"G","text":"incorporating"},{"label":"H","text":"reject"},{"label":"I","text":"balanced"},{"label":"J","text":"healthy"},{"label":"K","text":"abandon"},{"label":"L","text":"excessive"},{"label":"M","text":"images"},{"label":"N","text":"abandoned"},{"label":"O","text":"negative"}]',
