-- 选词填空 4: 城市化
('BANKED_CLOZE',
 '<p>Urbanization is accelerating at an unprecedented pace across the developing world. By 2050, it is <b>1._____</b> that nearly 70% of the global population will reside in urban areas. This demographic shift presents both remarkable opportunities and <b>2._____</b> challenges for sustainable development.</p><p>Cities are engines of economic growth, generating over 80% of global GDP. They attract <b>3._____</b> with the promise of better employment, education, and healthcare. However, rapid urban expansion often <b>4._____</b> existing infrastructure, leading to housing shortages, traffic congestion, and environmental degradation. The concept of "smart cities" has emerged as a potential <b>5._____</b>, using technology to improve urban services and quality of life. Sensors, data analytics, and artificial intelligence can help <b>6._____</b> traffic flow, reduce energy consumption, and enhance public safety. Yet critics warn that technological solutions alone cannot address the deep-seated <b>7._____</b> that plague many urban areas. Issues of affordable housing, social equity, and community <b>8._____</b> require thoughtful policy interventions. Successful urban development demands a <b>9._____</b> approach that combines technological innovation with social and environmental considerations. The cities that thrive in the coming decades will be those that <b>10._____</b> both efficiency and inclusivity.</p>',
 '[{"label":"A","text":"projected"},{"label":"B","text":"formidable"},{"label":"C","text":"migrants"},{"label":"D","text":"strains"},{"label":"E","text":"solution"},{"label":"F","text":"optimize"},{"label":"G","text":"inequalities"},{"label":"H","text":"cohesion"},{"label":"I","text":"holistic"},{"label":"J","text":"prioritize"},{"label":"K","text":"minor"},{"label":"L","text":"residents"},{"label":"M","text":"ignore"},{"label":"N","text":"complex"},{"label":"O","text":"temporary"}]',
 'A,B,C,D,E,F,G,H,I,J',
