('BANKED_CLOZE',
 '<p>Plastic pollution has emerged as one of the most <b>1._____</b> environmental crises of our era. An estimated 8 million tons of plastic waste enter the oceans each year, threatening marine <b>2._____</b> and human health. The problem is particularly acute in developing nations that lack adequate waste management <b>3._____</b>.</p><p>Microplastics—tiny particles less than 5mm in size—have been detected in the deepest ocean <b>4._____</b> and in the most remote Arctic ice. These particles are <b>5._____</b> by marine organisms and work their way up the food chain, ultimately reaching humans through seafood consumption. The long-term health <b>6._____</b> of this exposure are still being studied, but early research suggests cause for concern. Efforts to address the crisis have <b>7._____</b> on multiple fronts. Some countries have banned single-use plastics, while researchers are developing <b>8._____</b> materials that can decompose naturally. International organizations are working to establish a global <b>9._____</b> to coordinate action against plastic pollution. However, experts emphasize that technological solutions alone will not <b>10._____</b>; fundamental changes in production and consumption patterns are essential to stem the tide of plastic waste.</p>',
 '[{"label":"A","text":"pressing"},{"label":"B","text":"ecosystems"},{"label":"C","text":"infrastructure"},{"label":"D","text":"trenches"},{"label":"E","text":"ingested"},{"label":"F","text":"implications"},{"label":"G","text":"intensified"},{"label":"H","text":"biodegradable"},{"label":"I","text":"treaty"},{"label":"J","text":"suffice"},{"label":"K","text":"shallow"},{"label":"L","text":"ignored"},{"label":"M","text":"plastic"},{"label":"N","text":"neglected"},{"label":"O","text":"temporary"}]',
